{"step_index":1837,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-08-23T13:27:17Z","thinking":"**Examining IndexedDB Availability**\n\nI've confirmed that `window.indexedDB` is indeed a native feature, readily available in all modern browsers like Chrome, Safari, Firefox, and Edge. The implication is significant: we're dealing with a built-in component requiring no external dependencies for core functionality. Now I'm shifting focus to understanding its native mechanics.\n\n\n**Designing Data Storage Strategies**\n\nI'm now formulating strategies for utilizing IndexedDB's extensive storage capabilities. It's clear we can handle huge datasets, including binary data and Blobs, up to hundreds of gigabytes. My focus is on creating a rock-solid asynchronous IndexedDB storage adapter, with localStorage as a fallback. I'm also planning automatic data migration and backup/restore systems. I'm prioritizing user experience by handling image assets separately. This will avoid potential database bottlenecks.\n\n\n","tool_calls":[{"name":"view_file","args":{"AbsolutePath":"C:\\Users\\brorm\\.gemini\\antigravity\\scratch\\snap-dialer\\src\\screens\\SettingsScreen.tsx","EndLine":100,"StartLine":1,"toolAction":"Viewing SettingsScreen.tsx","toolSummary":"View SettingsScreen.tsx"}}]}
