{"step_index":1867,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-08-23T13:28:44Z","thinking":"**Refining Settings Screen**\n\nI'm currently working on incorporating the ShieldCheck icon into `SettingsScreen.tsx`. I've added state for `leadCount` and `logCount`. The `loadSettings` function is being refactored to fetch all leads and logs using `Promise.all` after importing and using the database.\n\n\n**Evaluating Storage Diagnostics**\n\nI've integrated the Storage Diagnostics Card into the UI. I added a section and a card in JSX to showcase the storage engine's health. It now displays different descriptions based on the platform and highlights the database type and safety features.\n\n\n","tool_calls":[{"name":"replace_file_content","args":{"AllowMultiple":false,"Description":"Add storage diagnostics and lead/log counts to SettingsScreen.tsx","EndLine":65,"Instruction":"Add storage engine diagnostics to SettingsScreen.tsx","ReplacementContent":"import {\n  ArrowLeft,\n  Key,\n  User,\n  Timer,\n  Cloud,\n  Download,\n  Share2,\n  Trash2,\n  Upload,\n  Copy,\n  Check,\n  Database,\n  X,\n  ShieldCheck,\n} from 'lucide-react-native';\nimport { SettingsRepository } from '../db/settingsRepository';\nimport { LeadsRepository } from '../db/leadsRepository';\nimport { BackupService, RestoreResult } from '../services/backupService';\nimport { HapticsService } from '../services/hapticsService';\nimport { Colors } from '../theme/colors';\n\nexport default function SettingsScreen({ navigation }: any) {\n  const [apiKey, setApiKey] = useState<string>('');\n  const [userName, setUserName] = useState<string>('Alex');\n  const [autoAdvanceEnabled, setAutoAdvanceEnabled] = useState<boolean>(true);\n  const [autoAdvanceSeconds, setAutoAdvanceSeconds] = useState<string>('3');\n  const [leadCount, setLeadCount] = useState<number>(0);\n  const [logCount, setLogCount] = useState<number>(0);\n\n  // Status Banners\n  const [savedBanner, setSavedBanner] = u